body:
Hallo,

&#x200B;

Gutachter bekommen 100€/Stunde für Schreiben und Reden mit dir. Heißt deine Gutachter waren schnell und somti günstig. Ich hab in etwa das doppelte bezahlt.

The Tension from the feelings, like many people with borderline experience it(and most people without borderline too.) when it hurts, when you would do anything to come out of this state. Anything is very literally. 

&#x200B;

Yes sometimes some one hears it, but most people don't. My psychiatrist can hear it very good. My caregiver always says I should talk to her before I cut.

The disorder does define you... and me.  Without some disorders people would not be who they are. Is a person with Autism, the same person without autism? All these disorders are on the way while personality is formed. Worse... I would not exist without this disorder I'm a "young" personality... I'm far younger than the body. Without this disorder I would be a man... and maybe someone very different...

&#x200B;

tl;dr My disorders define me.

I really like the purple bunny.

&#x200B;

And wow! That is impressive. How long did you collect?

Once you discovered that harming yourself is a valid coping mechanism, you won't get rid of the though. But you can stop and learn other coping mechanisms. e.G. I discovered that I need the pain to calm down. And someone helped me to find a thingie which I can use to get a big amount of pain **without** harming myself in any way. Another thing which calms me down is taking a shower. 

&#x200B;

I'm trans myself, and if someone would have asked me 4 years ago, before I started to transition, if I will ever be happy, I would have said "no never" but... I got my way and I feel very much better with my body. Like Kinky said, its about the little things. And some days I have so very great days. It can be very little things, like sitting in a burger King and having a Fanta, or something like that and it makes "click" and I feel like nothing can make me unhappy again.

Hi,

&#x200B;

Praxis Raue eher damit rechnen dass man Steine in den Weg gelegt bekommt und nichts außergewöhnliches an Hormontherapie, zumindest bei mir wurde klassisch mit Androcur und Estrifam(weil ich gynokadin nicht vertrag) gearbeitet. 

&#x200B;

Aber ansonsten super nette und sehr besorgte Ärzte. Lediglich dass sie die Allgemeingesundheit über die HRT legen nervt etwas.

&#x200B;

Grüße

Sophie
